// =============================================================================
// Chora Content Consumption — Companion concept/edge SUGGESTION events (ADR-212 WS-4)
// =============================================================================
//
// The learner-sovereign Discovery redesign (ADR-212 D4) demotes the ADR-143
// machine-authored "hexagonal fog" into a Companion-driven SUGGESTION engine: the
// LLM proposes candidate CONCEPTS + EDGES over the learner's sovereign map; the
// learner curates (Accept mints a real ConceptNode/Edge with
// provenance=companion_suggested_accepted; Dismiss declines). The dispatch is
// fully event-driven (feedback_agentic_pubsub_only): every agent invocation goes
// through Pub/Sub, orchestrator-managed.
//
// Flow:
//   1. chora-consumption publishes concept_suggestion.requested.v1 (learner asks
//      their bound Companion to suggest, via outbox) with the focal-concept
//      context + the existing concepts (so the fog does not re-propose them and
//      can reference them by id in proposed edges).
//   2. chora-fog-orchestrator (concept-shaped, ns ai-kernel) subscribes, runs the
//      LLM, and publishes concept_suggestion.emitted.v1 with the proposed
//      concepts + edges + the ADR-197 decision-stamps (model / run / tokens).
//   3. chora-consumption subscribes to emitted.v1 and persists each item as a
//      pending Suggestion (soft-cap, NOT exactly-6). Idempotent per envelope.
//
// Domain placement: per the topic-domain-follows-the-affected-aggregate-root
// convention (see weakness.proto header), BOTH events live in the `consumption`
// domain because the affected aggregate is the ConceptNode/Edge/Suggestion in
// chora_consumption — even though emitted.v1 is EMITTED by the ai-kernel fog
// orchestrator (the emitter does not determine the topic domain).
//
// Aggregate root : concept_suggestions / concept_nodes / concept_edges (chora_consumption)
// Owning domain  : Content Consumption (chora_consumption)
// Owning team    : Team 1 (Content)
// Topic prefix   : chora.consumption.concept_suggestion.*
// Surface        : A+ (Discovery map — suggestion chips)
//
// Subscribers:
//   - chora-fog-orchestrator (concept-suggestion crew) — subscribes to
//     concept_suggestion.requested.v1; runs the LLM; emits
//     concept_suggestion.emitted.v1.
//   - chora-consumption — subscribes to concept_suggestion.emitted.v1; persists
//     pending Suggestions (idempotent).
//   - chora-observability — D1 accountability + cost evidence on emitted.
// =============================================================================

